    "narrative": "For July 5th, Ghost Ride the WHIP leans heavily into high-upside speed and favorable pitching matchups to drive our 5x5 Roto metrics. The strongest play on the board is **James Wood** (76.28), who benefits from a prime leadoff spot and an elite 0.420 xwOBA against Chandler. Close behind, **Mickey Moniak** (75.98) and **Brice Turang** (75.06) provide elite efficiency; **Mickey Moniak** is buoyed by a significant +14% boost from a dynamic platoon advantage against Tyler Mahle, while **Brice Turang**\u2019s leadoff status and the slow delivery of Eduardo Rodriguez create an ideal environment for him to hunt stolen bases. **Corbin Carroll** (72.02) remains a cornerstone, though his score is slightly tempered by the risk of an elite hold pitcher.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved keeping **Travis Bazzana** (50.71) on the bench. While his +10% order bonus as a leadoff hitter is appealing, he was ultimately squeezed out by the efficiency of players like **Alex Freeland** and **Zach McKinstry** in the bottom of the order, who possess slightly higher composite projections when accounting for specific pitcher skill-sets today. We remain cautious regarding **Dalton Rushing**, whose score of 47.72 sits right at our marginal threshold; he faces JP Sears and is currently flagged with a \"Lineup Pending\" status, meaning we will need to monitor his final slotting to ensure the negative impact of an #8 or #9 position doesn't drag his efficiency below our floor. All starters should keep a close watch on **Seiya Suzuki**; his 63.79 score is strong, but a wind-in warning at the park could suppress his power output against Matthew Liberatore.",
